   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello, what does one here?<div><br></div><div>Thoughts on how to troubleshoot and next steps?<br><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><div>&gt; bear.scr &lt;- oSCR.fit(list(D ~ fruit + secure500, p0 ~ 1, sig ~ 1), </div><div>+                      ms.sf,                      # bear encounter data</div><div>+                      ms.ssDF,</div><div>+                      trimS=30E5)</div><div>Fitting model: D~fruit + secure500, p0~1, sigma~1, asu~1 </div><div>Using ll function &#39;msLL.sex&#39; </div><div>Hold on tight!</div><div>2019-07-11 13:40:14</div><div>p0.(Intercept) |  sig.(Intercept) |  d0.(Intercept) |  d.beta.fruit |  d.beta.secure500 |  psi.constant |  </div><div> </div><div>Error in solve.default(myfit$hessian) : </div><div>  system is computationally singular: reciprocal condition number = 5.19725e-22</div></div></code></div><br>Cheers,</div><div>Clayton</div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "-Ox7w7FoCgAJ",
   "from": "Daniel Linden",
   "author": "527d9b3ec7deff2d",
   "date": "2019-07-12T13:42:37Z",
   "subject": "Re: computationally singular",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Hey Clayton,</div><div><br></div><div>Can you share some plots of the covariates?  Histograms and maps?  If they aren&#39;t standardized and/or scaled well enough, that could be a problem.<br></div><div><br></div><div>The density model can be sensitive to the structure of the covariates and the amount of data (spatial recaptures, trapping extent, etc.).</div><div><br></div><div>Also, based on your trimS value it looks like you are working in meters.  Might be good to rescale to km.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
